---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Research" description="CFD research on bat flight using computational fluid-structure interaction at UTSI." currentPage="/research">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero__eyebrow">Research</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">Computational Fluid Dynamics</h1>
      <p class="hero__subtitle">
        Investigating how membrane perforations affect bat flight through
        fluid-structure interaction simulation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
    <div class="container">
      <!-- Affiliation -->
      <div class="card fade-in" style="margin-bottom:2rem; border-left:4px solid var(--accent);">
        <p style="margin:0; font-size:0.95rem;">
          <strong>Research Intern</strong> · University of Tennessee Space Institute<br />
          <span style="color:var(--text-secondary);">Advisor: Dr. Esteban Cisneros-Garibay · June 2026 – present</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview -->
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Research Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Bat wings are thin membranes that can sustain tears and perforations from encounters
          with obstacles, predators, or disease. Understanding how these holes affect aerodynamic
          performance is important for both biological modeling and the design of bio-inspired
          micro air vehicles.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work uses computational fluid-structure interaction (FSI) to simulate how membrane
          perforations change the flow field around flapping bat wings. I extended and validated
          an existing FSI codebase developed by Dr. Cisneros-Garibay's group, moving from a 2D
          flow model coupled with a 1D filament to full 3D flapping bat-wing models with
          membrane perforations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Simulation visual -->
      <div class="fade-in" style="margin:2rem 0;">
        <img src="/images/placeholder.png" alt="Bat-wing FSI simulation visualization" style="width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:var(--radius-md); object-fit:cover; max-height:400px;" />
      </div>

      <!-- Methods -->
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2>Methods &amp; Tools</h2>
        <p>
          The simulation framework uses <strong>Firedrake</strong> (finite element library built on PETSc)
          for spatial discretization, with meshes generated in <strong>Gmsh</strong> and results
          visualized in <strong>VisIt</strong>. Computations run on HPC clusters via <strong>Slurm</strong>.
        </p>

        <h3>Key Technical Contributions</h3>
        <ul style="padding-left:1.25rem; color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.8;">
          <li>Progressed from 2D flow + 1D filament model to 3D flapping bat-wing with membrane perforations</li>
          <li>Debugged mesh inversion issues in deforming geometries</li>
          <li>Fixed one-sided traction integral to a two-sided formulation for correct force coupling</li>
          <li>Implemented Gaussian envelope to suppress non-physical tip oscillation</li>
          <li>Validated solver against the Blasius flat-plate analytical solution</li>
          <li>Integrated energy-expenditure model (flow temperature, thermal balance, mechanical power)</li>
          <li>Extracted wing-boundary coordinates from a bat photograph for anatomically faithful mesh generation</li>
          <li>Studied numerical linear algebra: Krylov methods, GMRES, preconditioning, algebraic multigrid</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Current work -->
      <div class="fade-in" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h2>Current Work</h2>
        <p>
          I'm currently working on two-way FSI coupling and implementing leaky-filament
          boundary conditions to model injured wings with varying perforation sizes and
          locations. The goal is a parametric study connecting perforation geometry to
          aerodynamic performance degradation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Tech stack -->
      <div class="fade-in" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0.5rem; margin-top:0.75rem;">
          <span class="card__tag">Firedrake</span>
          <span class="card__tag">PETSc</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Python</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Gmsh</span>
          <span class="card__tag">VisIt</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Slurm / HPC</span>
          <span class="card__tag">Git / GitHub</span>
          <span class="card__tag">LaTeX / Beamer</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="fade-in" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <a href="/projects/bat-wing-fsi" class="btn btn--primary">View Full Project Detail →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
